<title>PORTUGAL: Yield eases on Portuguese six-month bills.</title>
<headline>Yield eases on Portuguese six-month bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield eased to 5.9564 percent, from 6.0882 percent previously, at the Treasury's sale of 182-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Treasury placed the 20 billion escudos after initially offering 15 billion. The last such sale was on December 11.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
